# Session scratch at the repo root. The convention already exists deeper in the
# tree (scripts/apifootball/_scratch/, scripts/uefa/_*); the root just never got
# the line, so one-off check scripts, verification screenshots and next-start
# logs have been sitting in `git status` since August.
_scratch/

# Commit messages staged for `git commit -F`. Written per push, never part of a
# commit, and 24 of them had accumulated at the root by 2026-08-13.
.commit-msg-*.txt

# Raw HTML scraped for the skyscraper pipeline. Regenerable, ~3.7 MB, and the
# parsed artifacts under public/data are what the site reads.
_supertalls-wiki.html
_tallest-buildings-wiki.html

# Excel source workbooks + Overture raw dumps: pipeline inputs on the Windows
# host, never read by `next build`. Kept on disk, out of git so Vercel does not
# clone ~50MB+ of them each deploy. Untrack existing ones with:
#   git rm --cached <file>   (keeps the working copy; reversible via history)
/*.xlsx
Overture-Match-Suggestions/*.xlsx
Overture-Per-Country-Raw/*.xlsx

# api-football pipeline scratch (contains apikey.txt + local data dumps) — never commit
scripts/apifootball/_scratch/
scripts/apifootball/__pycache__/


# uefa European-match archive: local scratch (regenerable crosswalk/dumps + parsed rows).
# The parser, loader, dump scripts and data/*.txt sources ARE tracked; only _-prefixed
# intermediates are ignored. Regenerate with dump_eursummary.py then parse_kassiesa.py.
scripts/uefa/_*
scripts/uefa/__pycache__/

# Large raw source (18.7 MB) for the pre-1993 English cup artifact. The compact artifact
# eng_cups_pre93.json and the builder build_eng_cups.py ARE tracked; keep this file locally to
# regenerate. (The German raw sources dfbpokal6092.txt / germanoberliga6063.txt are small and tracked.)
scripts/uefa/data/fa_league_cups.txt

# Mac mini job runtime. config.env holds real secrets (Supabase write key,
# EXCHANGERATE_API_KEY, REVALIDATE_SECRET) and needs its OWN line: the `.env*`
# rule above matches basenames starting with ".env", which "config.env" does
# not. config.env.example is the tracked template. state.json and the lock file
# are per-machine runtime state; dispatcher.log is already covered by *.log.
mac-mini-jobs/config.env
mac-mini-jobs/state.json
mac-mini-jobs/.dispatcher.lock
betatestkeys.txt

# Personal documents that happen to live in this working tree. This repo is
# PUBLIC, and git history keeps a file even after it is deleted, so anything
# private has to be stopped before the first commit rather than removed after.
# SAIS-Organization-Spotlight-Answers.md was committed here on 2026-08-13 and
# reset out again before it was ever pushed; this line is what stops the next
# `git add .` from doing it a second time.
SAIS-Organization-Spotlight-Answers.md

# Release-highlights reel working dir (screenshots, narration, music, cuts).
# Regenerate with scripts/reel/build_reel.py; the mp4 is a deliverable, not source.
reel-build/
